WEBVTT

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:39.120
Thank you, Kyoujyu!
These are the best Beys ever made!

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.130
You guys are amazing! To master the
Heavy Metal System so quickly...

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:51.130
The memory of my first day with a Beyblade helped me out!

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.780
Same for me!

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.600
So you guys figured it out too?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.460
The innocence we had back then...

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.120
I see! Controlling with with
your heart, not your head!

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.250
The source of your
love for Beyblade!

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:10.770
Yeah! The feeling I had
when I first got a Bey!

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.440
And I won't let BEGA get away with
trying to take that from us!

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.220
Let's do it, guys!

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.520
--Go, Shoot!

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.700
Okay! Go, Dragoon!

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.520
Now it's my turn!

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.420
Roar, Driger!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:39.130
Wow! These are the highest numbers they've produced!

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:44.020
The Heavy Metal System is more powerful
than I ever could have imagined!

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.330
Look at that!

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:53.700
Crap!

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.490
No! Daichi!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.620
What in the world?!

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.330
Watch it, will you?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.330
What if that had hit me?!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.160
Sorry.
It was an accident.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.000
If you mess up your timing
even a little, you'll lose control.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.130
These things aren't
a walk in the park.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.200
We have to stay focused.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:47.680
We can spin them thanks to the training camp,
but we still mess up about one third of the time.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.460
Despite the simpler design
of the Heavy Metal System,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.930
the Blader's abilities will
have a greater influence.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.660
If you're not 100% confident
or mess up even once...

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:06.820
It'll just lose control
and blow up?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:12.140
The problem is whether or not
we can perfect them in a match.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.930
Well, we shouldn't
think too much.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.530
We couldn't even spin
them before, but now we can!

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:25.570
We just have to make sure we
can control them by the match!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:29.220
That's why we have
to keep trying, Daichi!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.420
You dang kids!

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.690
Grandpa...

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.540
You think you're funny, do you?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:42.140
If you kids want to burn
off some excess energy...

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:46.100
Then line up! Your next
opponent is myself!

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.880
Oh yeah? Let's do it!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.860
No, Daichi!
Don't fight the elderly!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.930
No way! Grandpa's
a real monster!

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.370
I advise against it, Daichi!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.800
There's no way
we're a match for him!

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:05.100
Shut up! A man can never
back down from a challenge!

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.900
Well, sometimes
there are exceptions...

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.210
Jerk!

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:12.000
Everyone's so full of energy!

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.300
Looks like they're having fun
mastering new Beyblades.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:21.650
Which means they should be able to
perfectly control them before the match.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.570
Lemme go, Max!

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.970
Calm down Daichi!

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:32.000
They have to. They're the only ones who can use the Heavy Metal System to its full potential.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.160
Just them?

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:39.980
It's nice that they can
master the new Beys, but...

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.730
Our battle with BEGA is a
five VS five team battle.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.090
Gimme.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.650
Give you what?

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.340
You know what!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:56.320
I just don't believe that you guys are the
only ones who can use this Heavy-whatever.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.930
Don't forget, we're here too!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.130
Guys!

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:13.400
I'll get to the point.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.810
The Bladers participating in the
Justice 5 are confirmed, yes?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.920
Yes. But first, look at this.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.530
Thanks to the ID system, we can check the records of every Blader with ease.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.680
The top five based
on this data are...

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:44.010
Pros should be
evaluated on ability.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:48.010
Logically speaking, the
reps should be these five.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:02.920
But there's one who seems to
detest the idea of practice itself...

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.770
Geniuses are so carefree.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:12.130
But wasn't Brooklyn able to launch a
Beyblade thanks to your coaching?

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.800
I have faith that you
two can pull it off.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:20.500
One of BEGA's ideals is to dig
up hidden talent like his.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:27.340
So I think that relying on data might be a demotivator to everyone else.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.480
So everyone should
have an equal chance?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.020
Yes, and so...

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:37.610
Hey there,
future BEGA Bladers!

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:41.920
This is the five-on-five battle to
decide the future of Beyblading!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:45.450
The Justice 5 is in one week!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:52.530
Bladers who played in the world championships
are rumored to be fighting on his side!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:57.860
Who will be
on Kinomiya's team?

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:02.120
Their challengers will be an
elite squad of BEGA members!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.400
Who will be the ones
to defend BEGA?!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.450
In preparation for
next week's match,

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:20.000
there seems to be a contest going on
at BEGA HQ to choose their members!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.100
Let's go take a look!

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:33.660
We will now begin a tournament to decide the team for the Justice 5!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:38.570
You will be split in
blocks A through E.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.980
The winner of each
block will be chosen.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:48.210
But each block has a
high leveled Blader in it!

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:54.360
If you want to represent BEGA,
defeat them and win your way to the top!

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:01.100
So the result's
already clear, then!

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.520
Dang, Garland's in my block!

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:05.970
For real?

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.840
This is fixed!

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.300
Bladers!

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:14.810
Anyone who accepts defeat
before a match is no pro!

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:19.340
You are right to notice that
the top five Bladers stand out.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.520
But all of you have
an equal chance!

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:27.730
Those who take this once in a lifetime
chance will open a path of brilliant glory!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:32.440
That is the ideal of professionals.
Skill means everything!

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:37.050
That is true justice given
to all BEGA members!

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.610
He's right...

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.210
Let's do this!

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:42.840
We're all under the
same condition!

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:44.000
I can win!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.160
Now! Show me your
passionate Beyspirits!

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.900
You can make the
impossible possible!

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:07.440
--BEGA! BEGA! BEGA!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:09.640
Brooklyn and Kai?!

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:15.730
--BEGA! BEGA! BEGA!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.610
So that's it.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:26.990
--BEGA! BEGA! BEGA!

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:39.620
He's so pushy.
What a troublesome coach.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:43.060
Oh well.
Are you leaving, too?

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:15.920
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade G-Revolution"

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.130
Go!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:34.040
What's the big idea,
you crazy bull?!

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.840
I can't do it.
It won't listen to me!

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:41.010
I didn't think the Heavy Metal
System would be so tough.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:45.950
We can't even compare to them,
even though we fought on the same level?

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.800
What's the matter?

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.080
Rai, you need
to concentrate.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:56.690
Just blank out your mind! And focus
all your feeling into your Beyblade!

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:02.020
Don't blank out yours!

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.860
He's drooling!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.380
What?!

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.330
Like you can talk!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.080
I can't help but relax
around these guys...

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.140
Check this out, guys!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.860
They're doing a rep
tournament for BEGA!

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.440
What?!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.370
Do it! Don't lose!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.130
I did it, Monica!

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.470
Three.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.880
Two.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:53.730
One.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.900
Where's my opponent?

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:59.360
Here we go! Go, Shoot!

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.500
Go forth, Venus!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:21.330
Make these amateurs
vanish from sight!

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.180
Yay!

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.640
Aw, man...

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.050
I wooon~!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.100
Ming-Ming's the best!

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.290
What an idiot.

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:46.920
Is that the
best you can do?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.490
Darn...

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.370
Get lost!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.650
Apollon!

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.900
Wow!

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.450
They're crazy!

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:15.640
They must be confident if
they're showing this on live TV!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:17.410
Oh, Ming-Ming...

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:21.530
Garland has passed the
third round in the D block!

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:26.200
The A and B blocks are
approaching the finals!

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.760
They're rising
above all the rest.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.560
Their status as representatives
is all but confirmed.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:35.930
Yes, but if you
already knew that, sir...

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.380
What was the point of
holding this tournament?

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:43.680
The point?
Can you not see it?

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:48.400
Their drive to defeat an opponent beyond their skill level.

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:52.580
Their desire to take advantage
of even the smallest of chances.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.580
The days of ruling
Bladers by fear is over.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.170
Don't you agree?

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:05.160
Even the slightest bit of hope
can serve as motivation.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:12.660
By broadcasting this tournament, we can show people that BEGA has a system that's fair to everyone.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.280
Additionally, we might see
unknown Bladers show up who can

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:21.290
play circles around
the world champion.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:27.120
BEGA will have solid
ground to stand on.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:31.570
Those who believe they can become heroes will come running to BEGA.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.400
Yes.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.960
If that happens, we will have a firm
grasp on the world of Beyblading.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:43.680
An immense amount of fortune and fame,
power and influence is right around the corner.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:50.820
Moses wins the A block!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.370
Monica!!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.740
Mystel wins the B block!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:02.280
Ming-Ming wins the C block!

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.480
Yay!

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.960
Just a matter of time
until the D block ends!

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.250
They're all quite fast.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:18.320
What of our hero?

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.170
Take this seriously!

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.420
Are you makin' fun of me?

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.080
What? I'd never.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:39.860
Darn you!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:45.690
Whoopsie, what's Brooklyn doing?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.920
Beats me.

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:59.050
A Sleep Out!
Brooklyn wins!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.570
Crap!

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:06.920
It's time for the final
match of the E block!

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.130
Kai!

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:16.240
So Kai's the last one?

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.220
What's your game?

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:30.450
Are you making
fun of Beyblade?

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:34.850
It's boring.
I just didn't feel like it.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.540
So it's down to these two.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:44.450
Brooklyn is our secret weapon.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:51.880
But with his worthless practice data, he was just another one of our nameless members.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:58.580
He will fight Takao Kinomiya's
team in his glorious debut.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:06.730
The people will think that this a result of his BEGA membership and training.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:14.940
That is when he will become a star of
hope for Bladers all around the world.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:23.360
And for Kai Hiwatari to be the stepping stone for Brooklyn's big moment...

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:27.540
It is the greatest proof
of our impartiality!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:31.140
You have an impeccable knack for
storytelling, Coach Kinomiya.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.720
E block finals!

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:37.320
Three! Two! One!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:46.980
Brooklyn's Zeus lands in the
center and doesn't move!

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:49.980
Is he aiming for
another Sleep Out?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:54.880
He's screwing with me!
I'll force you to battle!

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:01.680
Hitoshi Kinomiya.

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:06.120
Show me just how
good your pupil is!

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:12.720
Go!
Dranzer Gigus Turbo!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.570
What's this?!

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.360
What?!

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.940
So you like
moves like those.

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.700
So...

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.770
What?!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.300
What was that?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.320
The same attack as Kai!

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.650
No way!

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:05.560
He copied my move!

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:08.500
Are you interested now?

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:11.920
Here we go.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:16.770
Kai Hiwatari. You're about
to get sent to hell.

00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:01.700
This is bad! Very bad!
The Justice 5 is about to begin!

00:23:01.700 --> 00:23:06.210
The future of Beyblading is riding on
these battles! We can't afford to lose!

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:09.000
More importantly, do we
have our fifth member?

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:11.970
Takao, Daichi, Rei, Max...
Who's the last one?

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:14.500
Umm, well, you see...

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:15.450
--Well?

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.200
Wait and see!

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.210
The mysterious champion, Mister X!

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:21.840
This isn't wrestling!
